  "problem": "Upon launching a new online course, the chief financial officer (CFO) of a company estimates that its profit, in thousands of dollars, is given by\n\n$$\nP(x)=0.3{x}^{3}-3.6{x}^{2}+10.8x+5,\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is the price, in dollars, of a single course. If the CFO estimates that the course price should be between $$1$ and $$7,$ at what price is the maximum profit obtained?\n\nThe profit is maximum when a single course costs $$$\n{{field-1}}.",
